#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every path listed here requires a signed X-Idp-Auth trailer on the HEAD commit that touches it.
# bin/idp-ci-guarded-paths enforces this server-side; the local pre-push hook echoes the same set.
# The rule: policy files, hook infrastructure, and this list itself cannot be changed without a
# founder signature. Cryptographic guarantee, not memory.
#
# Founder, 2026-11-13 (control-primitive lockdown): every file that tells an agent what it may do,
# or decides whether its work lands, is a control primitive. An agent may read one; it may never
# change one. W_agent(control primitives) = 0. A change lands only with the founder's X-Idp-Auth
# signature. Measured before this change: 49 commits touched these files on main from 2026-11-05
# to 2026-11-13, 44 of them landed by estate-agents[bot] with no founder signature (#8023, #8027
# and #8029 among them: agent-authored security workflows, merged unsigned within 90 minutes).
